questions.question:
Before the certificate call was moved to a background job, the first patch proposed for the incident was:

// api/certificates/client.ts
export const certClient = createHttpClient({
  baseUrl: "http://cert-svc.internal",
  timeoutMs: 2_000,                         // per attempt
  retry: { retries: 3, backoffMs: 200, factor: 2 },   // waits 200, 400, 800 ms
});

// POST /lessons/:id/complete still awaits certClient.post("/certificates", ...) inline

The certificate service hangs again: it accepts connections and never answers.

Statement: "With this patch, a hung certificate service can hold a POST /lessons/:id/complete request for at most about 2 seconds."
